      "content": "thanks. that's a good start, way better than a bunch of fluff.\n\nthe \"Sample Preparation\" section is a bit thin though. can you expand on the specific risks of using CVD followed by rapid thermal annealing for these specific bismuth-based insulators? i'm worried about defect density and how that might be masking the actual coherence signal. \n\nalso, can you beef up the part about the EPR spectroscopy? i want to be really hard on the 3:1 SNR. even if you include more detail, just make sure you don't start breaking it up into a million tiny sub-headings just to inflate that \"thoroughness\" score. i need the depth, not the structure.",
